[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m \[ 9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5 \times 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m We need to find the divisors of \(9!\) that end in 1, i.e., numbers congruent to 1 modulo 10. These divisors must be odd and congruent to 1 modulo 5. 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m We consider the odd part of the divisors, which are of the form \(3^a \times 5^b \times 7^c\) where \(0 \leq a \leq 4\), \(0 \leq b \leq 1\), and \(0 \leq c \leq 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m We need to check when \(3^a \times 5^b \times 7^c \equiv 1 \mod 10\). 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=464017)[0m 
